<title>PHILIPPINES: San Miguel B tumbles 5.43 pct.</title>
<headline>San Miguel B tumbles 5.43 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Beer maker San Miguel Corp's B shares fell five pesos, or 5.43 percent, to 87 pesos on Wednesday on concerns that an increase in its beer prices could adversely affect the company's profits, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Foreigners have been assessing the one peso price increase in San Miguel beer announced last week and there are concerns it may result in a drop in sales volume and therefore lead to a lower bottomline,&quot; said Helen Alvarez, research director at All Asia Securities.</p>
</text>
